rewritten-to-match
Same quicksort (middle pivot, Hoare-style partition, both halves recursed). Slices become index ranges (the language has none), and the per-run clone becomes a copy into a second array of the same size (the reference allocates a new Vec). Recursion stays within the 64-deep call limit for the run data. Other stores are range-checked; state is unlogged, so nothing is saved for a rollback. Scratch state rebuilt every run (the reference's locals: t) is not logged (state is unlogged by default, so no undo log, as a Rust local has none).
